<div class="mb-10"><h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Benchmarks</h1>
<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-6">Seven HTTP workloads, plus WebSockets &mdash; a JSON API response, a rendered HTML page, a database read, a database-backed HTML page, and one create, update and delete per request &mdash; through five full stacks on one machine, one load generator, one protocol. Every server returns a <strong class="text-white">byte-identical payload</strong> for the JSON and DB rows, and every stack runs <strong class="text-white">16 workers</strong>.</p>
<div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/5 p-5 mb-8"><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-amber-400">Read this first.</strong> Benchmarks are easy to rig and easy to get wrong. Everything below was measured in one session on a quiet box, after a warm-up pass over all nine endpoints, with the HTTP status of every response verified &mdash; and where Soli loses a cell, the number is printed exactly as measured. The per-operation Soli-vs-Ruby language tables that used to live on this page were retired with it; this page compares <em>frameworks</em>, end to end.</p></div></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Setup</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-6"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Soli</td><td class="py-3 px-4">1.25.0, <code class="text-cyan-400">soli serve .</code>, 16 HTTP workers, SoliDB (loopback HTTP) for the DB row</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Rails</td><td class="py-3 px-4">8.1.3 + Puma 8.0.2 on Ruby 3.4.9 &mdash; production, eager-loaded, 16 workers &times; 5 threads, PostgreSQL via ActiveRecord</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Laravel</td><td class="py-3 px-4">13.8 on PHP 8.4 (php-fpm, <code class="text-cyan-400">pm = static</code>, 16 workers) + nginx, in Docker with host networking &mdash; Eloquent + Blade, OPcache, config/route/view cached, persistent PDO connections. php-fpm, deliberately, not Octane</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Django</td><td class="py-3 px-4">6.0.7 on Python 3.14, gunicorn with 16 workers &mdash; Django ORM + Django templates, <code class="text-cyan-400">DEBUG=False</code>, persistent connections (<code class="text-cyan-400">CONN_MAX_AGE</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Express</td><td class="py-3 px-4">5.2.1 on Node 25.9, 16 cluster workers &mdash; <strong class="text-white">+ EJS 6.0 + Sequelize 6.37.8</strong> (on node-postgres 8.22): Express ships no view layer and no DB layer, both had to be added. The DB rows put it on an <strong class="text-white">ORM</strong>, not the raw driver, so all three stacks compare like for like; the driver number is kept below as a reference</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Database</td><td class="py-3 px-4">PostgreSQL 18.3 for Rails, Express, Laravel and Django (same table, same 50 rows); SoliDB for Soli &mdash; all client-server over a local socket, no in-process storage anywhere</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Load</td><td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-cyan-400">oha</code> 1.12 &mdash; 30s at concurrency 200 per cell, after an 8s warm-up of that cell</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-medium w-44">Machine</td><td class="py-3 px-4">16-core x86-64 Linux, load generator on the same box</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-gray-400 mb-8"><strong class="text-white">CPU/req</strong> is server CPU-time per request, summed across every process of the stack (all 17 for Rails, Express and Django; php-fpm plus nginx for Laravel). It is the most portable column here &mdash; unlike req/s it barely moves with core count or client speed.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">JSON &mdash; 50 objects, 2,268 bytes, built in the handler</h2>
<div class="mb-6" data-tabs>
<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1 mb-3" role="tablist"><button type="button" data-tab="result" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg bg-white/10 text-white font-medium transition" aria-selected="true">Result</button><button type="button" data-tab="soli" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Soli</button><button type="button" data-tab="rails" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Rails</button><button type="button" data-tab="express" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Express</button><button type="button" data-tab="laravel" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Laravel</button><button type="button" data-tab="django" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Django</button></div>
<div data-panel="result"><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-4"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Stack</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">req/s</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">p99</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">CPU/req</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">vs Rails</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Express + EJS + Sequelize</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">116,248</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6.17 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">106 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">7.3&times;</td></tr>
<tr class="bg-white/5"><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-bold">Soli</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white font-bold">77,452</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">5.99 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">173 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold">4.9&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Django + gunicorn</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">18,174</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">16.41 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">657 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.1&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Rails + Puma</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">15,838</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">25.28 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">913 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.0&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Laravel + php-fpm</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">6,208</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">36.95 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2,344 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">0.4&times;</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></div>
<div data-panel="soli" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-soli">def rows
  return (0..50).map(fn(i) {
    return { &quot;id&quot;: i + 1, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Post title #{i + 1}&quot;, &quot;views&quot;: (i + 1) * 7 }
  })
end

def json_only
  render_json(this.rows())
end</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="rails" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-ruby">def rows
  (1..50).map { |i| { id: i, title: &quot;Post title #{i}&quot;, views: i * 7 } }
end

def json_only
  render json: rows
end</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="express" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-javascript">const rows = () =&gt;
  Array.from({ length: 50 }, (_, i) =&gt;
    ({ id: i + 1, title: `Post title ${i + 1}`, views: (i + 1) * 7 }));

app.get(&#x27;/json&#x27;, (req, res) =&gt; res.json(rows()));</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="laravel" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-php">private function rows(): array
{
    $out = [];
    for ($i = 1; $i &lt;= 50; $i++) {
        $out[] = (object) [&#x27;id&#x27; =&gt; $i, &#x27;title&#x27; =&gt; &quot;Post title {$i}&quot;, &#x27;views&#x27; =&gt; $i * 7];
    }
    return $out;
}

public function jsonOnly() { return response()-&gt;json($this-&gt;rows()); }</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="django" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-python">def _rows():
    return [{&quot;id&quot;: i, &quot;title&quot;: f&quot;Post title {i}&quot;, &quot;views&quot;: i * 7} for i in range(1, 51)]


def json_only(request):
    # compact separators, or the payload is 299 bytes larger than everyone else&#x27;s
    return JsonResponse(_rows(), safe=False, json_dumps_params={&quot;separators&quot;: (&quot;,&quot;, &quot;:&quot;)})</code></pre></div>
</div>

<p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-8">Soli serialises the API response at 4.9&times; Rails' throughput on 5.3&times; less CPU. Express wins this row outright &mdash; printed as measured. Worth knowing: in Soli, serialising these 50 objects to JSON costs ~173&micro;s where rendering the <em>same data</em> as HTML costs 95&micro;s &mdash; the template engine is currently cheaper than <code class="text-cyan-400">render_json</code>.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Template &mdash; 50-row HTML table + layout, ~3 KB</h2>
<div class="mb-6" data-tabs>
<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1 mb-3" role="tablist"><button type="button" data-tab="result" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg bg-white/10 text-white font-medium transition" aria-selected="true">Result</button><button type="button" data-tab="soli" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Soli</button><button type="button" data-tab="rails" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Rails</button><button type="button" data-tab="express" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Express</button><button type="button" data-tab="laravel" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Laravel</button><button type="button" data-tab="django" class="px-3 py-1.5 text-sm rounded-lg text-gray-400 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/5 transition" aria-selected="false">Django</button></div>
<div data-panel="result"><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 mb-4"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4">Stack</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">req/s</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">p99</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">CPU/req</th><th class="py-3 px-4 text-right">vs Rails</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-gray-400 divide-y divide-white/10">
<tr class="bg-white/5"><td class="py-3 px-4 text-white font-bold">Soli</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-white font-bold">128,075</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">4.24 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-semibold">95 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-emerald-400 font-bold">11.6&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Express + EJS + Sequelize</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">67,249</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">7.87 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">198 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">6.1&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Rails + Puma</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">11,075</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">32.87 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1,188 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">1.0&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Django + gunicorn</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">7,194</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">34.53 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">1,946 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">0.6&times;</td></tr>
<tr><td class="py-3 px-4">Laravel + php-fpm</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">5,620</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">40.87 ms</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right">2,605 &micro;s</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-right text-gray-400">0.5&times;</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></div>
<div data-panel="soli" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-soli">def template_only
  render(&quot;posts/list&quot;, { &quot;title&quot;: &quot;Posts&quot;, &quot;items&quot;: this.rows() })
end</code></pre></div>
<div data-panel="rails" class="hidden"><pre class="bg-black/40 border border-white/10 rounded-xl p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="language-ruby">def template_only
  @title = &quot;Posts&quot;
  render &quot;posts/list&quot;, locals: { items: rows }
end</code></pre></div>
